descr":"Il y a six si\u00e8cles, Bruxelles appartenait aux souverains les plus riches et les plus puissants d\u2019Europe les ducs de Bourgogne. Fins politiques et m\u00e9c\u00e8nes cultiv\u00e9s, ils se sont constitu\u00e9 un \u00e9mouvant tr\u00e9sor : une collection de manuscrits tellement unique qu\u2019elle a son propre nom, la Librairie des ducs de Bourgogne.\r\n\r\nCes chefs-d\u2019oeuvre, rescap\u00e9s des outrages du temps et de l\u2019Histoire, KBR les prot\u00e8ge pour vous. Il ouvre aujourd\u2019hui ses coffres pour en partager les cl\u00e9s et les splendeurs \u00e0 travers son nouveau mus\u00e9e.\r\n\r\nSi tout le monde connait aujourd\u2019hui Jan Van Eyck ou Rogier van der Weyden, les miniaturistes, peintres des livres, n\u2019avaient rien \u00e0 leur envier. Au point de faire dire \u00e0 certains que les plus beaux tableaux des Primitifs flamands se trouvent peut-\u00eatre dans les manuscrits.\r\n\r\nLa Librairie est une incroyable collection \u00e0 laquelle nous vous donnons acc\u00e8s au c\u0153ur du nouveau mus\u00e9e.\r\n\r\nNous vous raconterons les histoires de ces livres et l\u2019\u00e9poque qui les a vus na\u00eetre. Vous d\u00e9couvrirez ainsi qu\u2019il est pr\u00e9f\u00e9rable de se m\u00e9fier des lapins, que le Moyen \u00c2ge est \u00e0 mourir de rire, qu\u2019on a vu des sir\u00e8nes \u00e0 Bruxelles ou que les livres d\u2019histoire  mentent parfois.\r\n\r\nPlus d'information: www.kbr.be\/fr\/museum\r\n\r\nOuvert du mardi au dimanche : 10:00 \u2013 17:00\r\nFerm\u00e9 le lundi et certains jours f\u00e9ri\u00e9s (1er janvier, dimanche et lundi de P\u00e2ques, 1er mai, jeudi de l\u2019ascension, lundi de Pentec\u00f4te, 21 juillet, 15 ao\u00fbt, 1er novembre, 11 novembre, 25 d\u00e9cembre)","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be\/fr\/museum","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"nl":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":"Belgi\u00eb verbergt al 600 jaar een schat: de Librije van de Bourgondische hertogen. Kom deze unieke verzameling handschriften nu ontdekken in het KBR museum.","longdescr":"Zeshonderd jaar geleden regeerden de hertogen van Bourgondi\u00eb over Brussel. Deze rijke en machtige vorsten en gecultiveerde mecenassen stelden een schat samen die ook vandaag nog weet te boeien: de Librije, een verzameling handschriften die zo uniek is dat ze haar eigen naam kreeg.\r\n\r\nHeel wat van deze meesterwerken wisten de tand des tijds te doorstaan en worden door KBR voor u gekoesterd. Vandaag openen we onze schatkist en delen we deze pareltjes met u in en rond de Nassaukapel.\r\n\r\nIedereen kent Jan Van Eyck of Rogier van der Weyden, maar de miniaturisten die de handschriften verluchtten moesten zeker niet voor hen onderdoen. Sommigen beweren zelfs dat de mooiste schilderijen van de Vlaamse primitieven misschien wel die zijn die we in de handschriften terugvinden.\r\n\r\nHet zijn deze handschriften die het hart van het nieuwe museum vormen.\r\n\r\nOntdek de geschiedenis van deze boeken en de periode waarin ze tot stand kwamen. Ontdek waarom u konijnen moet wantrouwen, dat er zeemeerminnen gespot zijn in Brussel en dat geschiedenisboeken soms wel eens durven te liegen.\r\n\r\nMeer informatie: www.kbr.be\/nl\/museum\r\n\r\nOpen van dinsdag tot zondag van 10.00 tot 17.00 uur.\r\nGesloten op maandag en sommige feestdagen (1 januari, Paaszondag, Paasmaandag, 1 mei, donderdag van Onze Heer Hemelvaart, Pinkstermaandag, 21 juli, 15 augustus, 1 november, 11 november, 25 december)","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be\/nl\/museum","email":"info@kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"en":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":"Belgium has been hiding a treasure for 600 years: the manuscripts of the Dukes of Burgundy. Come discover these fabulous masterpieces rescued from time at the KBR museum.","longdescr":"Six centuries ago, Brussels belonged to the rich and powerful Dukes of Burgundy. Skilled politicians and cultured patrons, they established a stirring treasure, a unique and fascinating collection of manuscripts: the Library of the Dukes of Burgundy.\r\n\r\nThese masterpieces, which have survived the ravages of time and of history, have been looked after for you by KBR. It is now opening its vaults to share the highlights of this fantastic collection via its new museum. The sixteenth-century Chapel of Nassau and the various rooms that surround it will form the backdrop to the museum.\r\n\r\nThe museum offers you the opportunity to share in Europe\u2019s medieval cultural past, and admire beautiful illuminated manuscripts.\r\n\r\nThese days, everyone knows about Jan Van Eyck and Rogier van der Weyden, but the miniature artists, responsible for producing illuminated manuscripts, are every bit as impressive. So much so that some say that the finest Flemish Primitive paintings can perhaps be found in manuscripts.\r\n\r\nIt is these original manuscripts that are at the heart of the new museum.\r\n\r\nWe will tell you the history of these books and the era that produced them. You will find out why you shouldn\u2019t trust rabbits, in what way the Middle Ages were hilarious, how mermaids were spotted in Brussels, and discover how history books sometimes lie\u2026\r\n\r\nMore information: www.kbr.be\/en\/museum\r\n\r\nOpen Tuesday to Sunday, 10 am \u2013 5 pm\r\nClosed on Mondays and 1 January, Easter and Monday 15 August, 1 May, Ascension Day, Whit Monday, 21 July, 15 August, 1 November, 11 November, 25 December","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be\/en\/museum","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"de":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"it":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"sp":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"pt":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"},"cn":{"name":"KBR museum","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.504860"}},"place":{"id":981,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"En 1839, la Biblioth\u00e8que royale de Belgique se situait dans le Palais de Charles de Lorraine. Celui-ci accueille d\u00e9sormais les expositions temporaires de KBR. En plus d'y d\u00e9couvrir des documents exceptionnels, vous pourrez \u00e9galement admirer toute la beaut\u00e9 du lieu. Le palais est accessible aux personnes \u00e0 mobilit\u00e9 r\u00e9duite.\r\nLorsqu\u2019il n\u2019y a pas d\u2019exposition en cours, vous pouvez louer les appartements et la rotonde pour des \u00e9v\u00e9nements.\r\n\r\nHistoire du b\u00e2timent\r\nCharles de Lorraine fut gouverneur g\u00e9n\u00e9ral des Pays-Bas autrichiens de 1744 \u00e0 1780. Avide de connaissances dans le domaine des sciences, admirateur de l\u2019Encyclop\u00e9die de Diderot et d\u2019Alembert, il \u00e9tait \u00e9galement un grand amateur d\u2019art et un collectionneur passionn\u00e9.\r\nLa construction du Palais de Charles de Lorraine d\u00e9buta en 1757, sur le site de l'ancien palais de Nassau dont les seuls t\u00e9moins actuels sont la fa\u00e7ade de style rocaille tardif\/d\u00e9but du n\u00e9o-classicisme et les \u00e9l\u00e9ments d\u00e9coratifs, sculpt\u00e9s par Laurent Delvaux. La majestueuse statue d'Hercule en marbre blanc, figurant au pied de l'escalier int\u00e9rieur du palais est \u00e9galement de la main de cet artiste. Le superbe sol de marbre de la rotonde, de style italien, est d\u00e9cor\u00e9 d'une rose compos\u00e9e des \u00e9chantillons des diff\u00e9rentes vari\u00e9t\u00e9s de marbre de nos r\u00e9gions. La rotonde vous m\u00e8ne aux appartements : cinq pi\u00e8ces adjacentes, orn\u00e9es de somptueux parquets, de lustres majestueux et de riches \u00e9toffes.\r\n\r\nPlus d\u2019info : https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/fr\/lieu\/palais-de-charles-de-lorraine\/\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Kunstberg","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Kunstberg","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"In 1839 was de Koninklijke Bibliotheek gelegen in het Paleis van Karel van Lotharingen. Nu is het 18de-eeuwse paleis het decor voor de tijdelijke tentoonstellingen van KBR. Daarbuiten is het enkel toegankelijk tijdens speciale evenementen. Het paleis is volledig toegankelijk voor personen met beperkte mobiliteit.\r\nWanneer er geen tentoonstelling loopt, kunt u de appartementen en de rotonde huren voor evenementen. \r\n \r\nGeschiedenis van het gebouw\r\nKarel van Lotharingen was de gouverneur-generaal van de Oostenrijkse Nederlanden van 1744 tot 1780. Hij was een leergierig man op gebied van de wetenschappen en het occultisme, een kenner van de Encyclop\u00e9die van Diderot en d\u2019Alembert, kunstliefhebber en verwoed verzamelaar.\r\nHet Paleis van Karel van Lotharingen werd vanaf 1757 gebouwd op de plek waar vroeger het paleis van Nassau stond. Er bestaat alleen nog een gevel uit het laat-rocaille en begin neo-classicisme met decoratieve elementen van Laurent Delvaux. Het marmeren beeld van Hercules in het trappenhuis is eveneens het werk van Delvaux. De rotonde in Italiaanse stijl is versierd met een prachtige marmeren vloer waarin stalen van marmersoorten uit onze gewesten zijn ingevoegd. De rotonde leidt u naar de appartementen: vijf aan elkaar grenzende vertrekken met prachtige parketvloeren, majestueuze kroonluchters en indrukwekkend gedrapeerde gordijnen.\r\n \r\nMeer info: https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/nl\/locatie\/paleis-van-karel-van-lotharingen\/\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"In 1839, the Royal Library of Belgium was housed in the Palace of Charles of Lorraine. Today, the Palace hosts KBR\u2019s temporary exhibitions. You can only enter the palace during these exhibitions or at special events. The palace is entirely wheelchair accessible.\r\nWhen there is no exhibition running, you can rent the apartments and the rotunda for events.\r\n \r\nHistory of this building\r\nCharles of Lorraine was the governor of the Austrian Netherlands from 1744 to 1780. He was an avid art and science enthusiast and collector. His palace, the construction of which started in 1757, later housed the Royal Library's reading rooms and is now used for events and exhibitions.\r\n \r\nAn impressive staircase, adorned with a statue of Hercules, sculpted by Laurent Delvaux, leads up to the first-floor rotunda. The rotunda's paving includes a central rosette made up of 28 types of Belgian marble, a sample of the Prince's collection of 5,000 minerals. The rotunda's wonderful floor art leads to five rooms decorated with stuccos and silk, where the governor used to entertain his guests and took care of state affairs.\r\n\r\nMore information: https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/en\/venue\/palace-of-charles-of-lorraine\/\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[16],"translations":{"fr":["Quartier Royal"],"nl":["Koninklijke wijk"],"en":["Royal"]}},"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"fr":["Centre"],"nl":["Centrum"],"en":["Centre"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":170,"location":{"lat":50.84321233,"lon":4.35747449},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-08-08T01:06:33+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:19+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":981,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"En 1839, la Biblioth\u00e8que royale de Belgique se situait dans le Palais de Charles de Lorraine. Celui-ci accueille d\u00e9sormais les expositions temporaires de KBR. En plus d'y d\u00e9couvrir des documents exceptionnels, vous pourrez \u00e9galement admirer toute la beaut\u00e9 du lieu. Le palais est accessible aux personnes \u00e0 mobilit\u00e9 r\u00e9duite.\r\nLorsqu\u2019il n\u2019y a pas d\u2019exposition en cours, vous pouvez louer les appartements et la rotonde pour des \u00e9v\u00e9nements.\r\n\r\nHistoire du b\u00e2timent\r\nCharles de Lorraine fut gouverneur g\u00e9n\u00e9ral des Pays-Bas autrichiens de 1744 \u00e0 1780. Avide de connaissances dans le domaine des sciences, admirateur de l\u2019Encyclop\u00e9die de Diderot et d\u2019Alembert, il \u00e9tait \u00e9galement un grand amateur d\u2019art et un collectionneur passionn\u00e9.\r\nLa construction du Palais de Charles de Lorraine d\u00e9buta en 1757, sur le site de l'ancien palais de Nassau dont les seuls t\u00e9moins actuels sont la fa\u00e7ade de style rocaille tardif\/d\u00e9but du n\u00e9o-classicisme et les \u00e9l\u00e9ments d\u00e9coratifs, sculpt\u00e9s par Laurent Delvaux. La majestueuse statue d'Hercule en marbre blanc, figurant au pied de l'escalier int\u00e9rieur du palais est \u00e9galement de la main de cet artiste. Le superbe sol de marbre de la rotonde, de style italien, est d\u00e9cor\u00e9 d'une rose compos\u00e9e des \u00e9chantillons des diff\u00e9rentes vari\u00e9t\u00e9s de marbre de nos r\u00e9gions. La rotonde vous m\u00e8ne aux appartements : cinq pi\u00e8ces adjacentes, orn\u00e9es de somptueux parquets, de lustres majestueux et de riches \u00e9toffes.\r\n\r\nPlus d\u2019info : https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/fr\/lieu\/palais-de-charles-de-lorraine\/\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Kunstberg","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Kunstberg","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"In 1839 was de Koninklijke Bibliotheek gelegen in het Paleis van Karel van Lotharingen. Nu is het 18de-eeuwse paleis het decor voor de tijdelijke tentoonstellingen van KBR. Daarbuiten is het enkel toegankelijk tijdens speciale evenementen. Het paleis is volledig toegankelijk voor personen met beperkte mobiliteit.\r\nWanneer er geen tentoonstelling loopt, kunt u de appartementen en de rotonde huren voor evenementen. \r\n \r\nGeschiedenis van het gebouw\r\nKarel van Lotharingen was de gouverneur-generaal van de Oostenrijkse Nederlanden van 1744 tot 1780. Hij was een leergierig man op gebied van de wetenschappen en het occultisme, een kenner van de Encyclop\u00e9die van Diderot en d\u2019Alembert, kunstliefhebber en verwoed verzamelaar.\r\nHet Paleis van Karel van Lotharingen werd vanaf 1757 gebouwd op de plek waar vroeger het paleis van Nassau stond. Er bestaat alleen nog een gevel uit het laat-rocaille en begin neo-classicisme met decoratieve elementen van Laurent Delvaux. Het marmeren beeld van Hercules in het trappenhuis is eveneens het werk van Delvaux. De rotonde in Italiaanse stijl is versierd met een prachtige marmeren vloer waarin stalen van marmersoorten uit onze gewesten zijn ingevoegd. De rotonde leidt u naar de appartementen: vijf aan elkaar grenzende vertrekken met prachtige parketvloeren, majestueuze kroonluchters en indrukwekkend gedrapeerde gordijnen.\r\n \r\nMeer info: https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/nl\/locatie\/paleis-van-karel-van-lotharingen\/\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"In 1839, the Royal Library of Belgium was housed in the Palace of Charles of Lorraine. Today, the Palace hosts KBR\u2019s temporary exhibitions. You can only enter the palace during these exhibitions or at special events. The palace is entirely wheelchair accessible.\r\nWhen there is no exhibition running, you can rent the apartments and the rotunda for events.\r\n \r\nHistory of this building\r\nCharles of Lorraine was the governor of the Austrian Netherlands from 1744 to 1780. He was an avid art and science enthusiast and collector. His palace, the construction of which started in 1757, later housed the Royal Library's reading rooms and is now used for events and exhibitions.\r\n \r\nAn impressive staircase, adorned with a statue of Hercules, sculpted by Laurent Delvaux, leads up to the first-floor rotunda. The rotunda's paving includes a central rosette made up of 28 types of Belgian marble, a sample of the Prince's collection of 5,000 minerals. The rotunda's wonderful floor art leads to five rooms decorated with stuccos and silk, where the governor used to entertain his guests and took care of state affairs.\r\n\r\nMore information: https:\/\/www.kbr.be\/en\/venue\/palace-of-charles-of-lorraine\/\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"KBR museum","address_street_name":"Mont des Arts","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kbr.be","website":"http:\/\/www.kbr.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 519 53 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Mont des Arts","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null