\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9"],"nl":["Toegankelijk voor mensen met een verstandelijke beperking","Toegankelijk","Toegankelijke parking","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Accessible","Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-08-08T01:07:33+02:00","published_at":"2022-02-04T17:32:58+01:00","backoffice_id":246911,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.20445828459884},{"id":526883,"date_start":"2022-02-03","date_end":"2022-09-25","date_next":"2022-08-11","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,42],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Peinture"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Schilderkunst"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Painting"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["nl","fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Du priv\u00e9 au public. Collection Thomas Neirynck, du sentiment \u00e0 l'expression lyrique","shortdescr":"Un collectionneur priv\u00e9 qui fait don de l\u2019\u0153uvre de sa vie pour la montrer au public. La collection du m\u00e9c\u00e8ne Thomas Neirynck offre une vision subjective de l\u2019art abstrait de la seconde moiti\u00e9 du 20e si\u00e8cle.\r\nUne s\u00e9lection d\u2019\u0153uvres qui pr\u00e9sente de grands et de moins grands noms de l\u2019art, tous des intimes de Neirynck, allant des post-expressionnistes \u00e0 divers artistes abstraits.","longdescr":"'Du priv\u00e9 au public' offre un regard sur une manie de collectionneur qui a vu le jour et a \u00e9t\u00e9 inspir\u00e9e imm\u00e9diatement apr\u00e8s la fin de la Seconde Guerre mondiale. Thomas Neirynck \u00e9tait un enfant de son temps, vivant cette guerre comme un jeune homme de vingt ans, ce qui se refl\u00e8te dans le choix de ses \u0153uvres d'art. Il recherchait des \u0153uvres qui entraient en r\u00e9sonnance avec son v\u00e9cu, qui exprimaient son besoin de renouveau et de modernit\u00e9, des \u0153uvres qu'il aurait peut-\u00eatre aim\u00e9 peindre lui-m\u00eame. En ce sens, il \u00e9tait un amateur au sens propre du terme, anim\u00e9 par la passion, le sentiment et la fascination pour l'artiste. \r\nDes \u0153uvres grandes et dignes d'Antoine Mortier, des toiles color\u00e9es de Maurice Wyckaert, des tableaux all\u00e9goriques de Fred Bervoets, des \u0153uvres exub\u00e9rantes de Philippe Vandenberg et des \u0153uvres po\u00e9tiques de Jo Delahaut. Mais aussi des \u0153uvres d'artistes moins connus, tels que Tal Coat, Yvan Theys, Andr\u00e9 Lanskoy, Jacques Doucet et Lionel Vinche. Une grande partie de la collection provient de la maison du collectionneur. Le FeliXart Museum replace une s\u00e9lection de la collection dans son \u00e9poque et l'\u00e9value en fonction des valeurs qu'elle rev\u00eat aujourd'hui. En exposant dans un mus\u00e9e des \u0153uvres d'art provenant \u00e0 l'origine d'une collection priv\u00e9e, la perception change et elles gagnent en grandeur.","performers":"Maurice Wyckaert, Antoine Mortier, Philippe Vandenberg, Fred Bervoets, Jo Delahaut, Gilbert De Cock, Asger Jorn, Karel Appel, Pierre Alechinsky, Guy Vandenbranden, Arman, Pierre Soulages, Louis Van Lint, Bram Bogart, Georges Mathieu,...","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"nl":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":"Een priv\u00e9-verzamelaar die zijn levenswerk schonk om het aan het publiek te tonen. De collectie van mecenas Thomas Neirynck geeft een subjectieve kijk op abstracte kunst uit de tweede helft van de 20ste eeuw.\r\nWeinig getoonde werken van grote en minder grote namen, allen intimi van Neirynck, gaande van post-expressionisten tot diverse abstracte kunstenaars.","longdescr":"\u2018Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek\u2019 werpt een blik op een verzamelwoede die zijn oorsprong en inspiratie kent meteen na het einde van de Tweede Wereldoorlog. Thomas Neirynck was een kind van zijn tijd, beleefde deze oorlog als jonge twintiger, wat zich uit in zijn keuze van kunstwerken. Hij zocht naar vernieuwing, naar kunstenaars die de vrijheid van expressie voorop stelden en die het onvatbare van de oorlogsjaren achter zich wilden laten. In die zin was hij een amateur in de ware zin van het woord, gedreven door passie, sentiment en fascinatie voor de kunstenaar.\r\nGrote en waardige werken van Antoine Mortier, kleurrijke doeken van Maurice Wijckaert, allegorische schilderijen van Fred Bervoets, uitbundige werken van Philippe Vandenberg en po\u00ebtische werken van Jo Delahaut. Maar ook kunstwerken van minder bekende kunstenaars, zoals Tal Coat, Yvan Theys, Andr\u00e9 Lanskoy, Jacques Doucet, Lionel Vinche. Een groot stuk van de collectie komt uit de huiselijke sfeer van de verzamelaar. Het FeliXart Museum plaatst een selectie uit de collectie in haar tijd en beoordeeld de verzameling naar de waardes die ze vandaag nog heeft. Door de kunstwerken die oorspronkelijk uit een priv\u00e9collectie komen tentoon te stellen in een museale ruimte, verschuift de perceptie en krijgen ze grandeur.","performers":"Maurice Wyckaert, Antoine Mortier, Philippe Vandenberg, Fred Bervoets, Jo Delahaut, Gilbert De Cock, Asger Jorn, Karel Appel, Pierre Alechinsky, Guy Vandenbranden, Arman, Pierre Soulages, Louis Van Lint, Bram Bogart, Georges Mathieu,...","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","email":"info@felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":"+32 2 377 57 22","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"en":{"name":"From private to public. Collection Thomas Neirynck, from sentiment to lyrical expression","shortdescr":"A private collector who donated his life\u2019s work to show it to the public. The collection of patron Thomas Neirynck gives a subjective view of abstract art from the second half of the 20th century.\r\nSelected works of great and less great names, all intimates of Neirynck, ranging from post-expressionists to various abstract artists","longdescr":"'From private to public' casts a glance at a collector's mania that had its origin and inspiration immediately after the end of the Second World War. Thomas Neirynck was a child of his time, experiencing this war as a young twenty-something, which is reflected in his choice of works of art. He was looking for innovation, for artists who put freedom of expression first and who wanted to leave the intangible of the war years behind them. In that sense, he was an amateur in the true sense of the word, driven by passion, sentiment and fascination for the artist.\r\nLarge and dignified works by Antoine Mortier, colourful canvases by Maurice Wyckaert, allegorical paintings by Fred Bervoets, exuberant works by Philippe Vandenberg and poetic works by Jo Delahaut. But also works of art by less well-known artists, such as Tal Coat, Yvan Theys, Andr\u00e9 Lanskoy, Jacques Doucet and Lionel Vinche. A large part of the collection comes from the collector's home. The FeliXart Museum places a selection from the collection in its time and assesses it according to the values it holds today. By exhibiting the works of art that originally came from a private collection in a museum space, the perception shifts and they gain grandeur.","performers":"Maurice Wyckaert, Antoine Mortier, Philippe Vandenberg, Fred Bervoets, Jo Delahaut, Gilbert De Cock, Asger Jorn, Karel Appel, Pierre Alechinsky, Guy Vandenbranden, Arman, Pierre Soulages, Louis Van Lint, Bram Bogart, Georges Mathieu,...","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"de":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"it":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"sp":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"pt":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"},"cn":{"name":"Van priv\u00e9 naar publiek. Collectie Thomas Neirynck, van sentiment naar lyrische epressie","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.526883"}},"place":{"id":248774,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"Dans un endroit inattendu, au centre de la commune urbanis\u00e9e de Drogenbos, se trouve le FeliXart Museum, entour\u00e9 d\u2019une oasis de verdure de 5ha. Ce domaine appartenait \u00e0 Felix De Boeck (1898-1995), l\u2019un des pionniers de l\u2019art abstrait en Belgique. Le mus\u00e9e a ouvert ses portes en 1996 et se concentre sur l\u2019art abstrait des avant-gardes historiques, l\u2019art contemporain ainsi que sur les questions de perception visuelle. Gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 diff\u00e9rents projets, dont des expositions et des publications d\u2019importance nationale et internationale, le mus\u00e9e a d\u00e9velopp\u00e9 une r\u00e9elle expertise sur le sujet et a pris, ces derni\u00e8res ann\u00e9es, une place de plus en plus remarqu\u00e9e au sein des institutions mus\u00e9ales.\r\n\r\nLe mus\u00e9e fonctionne avec deux grands volets. D\u2019une part, il y a FeliXeco, le volet \u00e9cologique, qui se d\u00e9ploie principalement entre les arbres sur le magnifique domaine vert du mus\u00e9e. D\u2019autre part, il y a FeliXart, la partie artistique de l\u2019organisation. L\u2019ART dans FeliXart repr\u00e9sente trois plateformes : Aspects, R\u00e9flexions et Talents. Un triptyque sur lequel le mus\u00e9e travaille pour garder l\u2019art vivant et continuer \u00e0 surprendre le visiteur. N\u00e9anmoins, le travail de Felix forme le fil conducteur, la qualit\u00e9 et l\u2019authenticit\u00e9 sont les crit\u00e8res les plus importants. L\u2019objectif est d\u2019actualiser et de contextualiser l\u2019\u0153uvre du peintre-fermier.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"Op een plek waar je het niet verwacht, in het centrum van de kleine verstedelijkte gemeente Drogenbos, ligt het FeliXart museum, in een oase van 5ha groen, het domein dat ooit van Felix De Boeck (1895-1995) was, een van de pioniers van de Belgische abstracte kunst. Het museum opende in 1996 en focust zich op historische en hedendaagse avant-gardekunst. Dankzij tentoonstellingen, projecten en publicaties van nationale en internationale uitstraling heeft het museum de laatste jaren een belangrijke plaats ingenomen binnen de expertise rond avant-garde, Interbellum en abstracte kunst.\r\n\r\nHet museum werkt met twee grote luiken. Enerzijds is het er FeliXeco, het ecologische luik, dat zich voornamelijk ontplooit tussen de bomen op het prachtige groene domein van het museum. Daarnaast is er FeliXart, het artistieke luik van de organisatie. De ART in FeliXart staat voor drie platformen: Aspecten, Reflecties en Talenten. Een drieluik waarop het museum inzet om kunst in leven te houden en de bezoeker te blijven verrasssen. Het werk van Felix vormt niettemin de rode draad, kwaliteit en authenticiteit zijn de belangrijkste criteria. Actualisering en contextualisering van het oeuvre van de schilder-boer zijn het doel.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"In a place where you wouldn\u2019t expect it, in the centre of the small urbanised municipality of Drogenbos, the FeliXart museum is situated in an oasis of 5 hectares of green, the domain that once belonged to Felix De Boeck (1895-1995), one of the pioneers of Belgian abstract art. The museum opened in 1996 and focuses on historical and contemporary avant-garde art. Thanks to exhibitions, projects and publications of national and international standing, the museum has in recent years occupied an important place within the expertise on avant-garde, Interbellum and abstract art.\r\n\r\nThe museum works with two large panels. On the one hand there is FeliXeco, the ecological hatch, which mainly unfolds between the trees on the beautiful green domain of the museum. On the other hand there is FeliXart, the artistic part of the organisation. The ART in FeliXart stands for three platforms: Aspects, Reflections and Talents. A triptych on which the museum works to keep art alive and continue to surprise the visitor. Nevertheless, Felix\u2019s work forms the common thread, quality and authenticity are the most important criteria. The aim is to update and contextualise the oeuvre of the painter-farmer.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"FeliXart Museum","address_street_name":"Kuikenstraat","address_street_number":"6","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.felixart.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 377 57 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1620","address_city":"Drogenbos","address_line1":"Kuikenstraat, 6","address_line2":"1620 Drogenbos","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":[],"zones":{"list":[999],"translations":{"fr":["Autour de Bruxelles"],"nl":["Rond Brussel"],"en":["Around Brussels"]}},"tags":["force_publication"],"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":10930,"location":{"lat":50.7893747,"lon":4.3147533},"region":"flanders","last_updated_at":"2022-08-08T01:07:30+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:29:23+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_ad